# Google Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) / mtalk
# Community rule set for FCM push endpoints (TCP 443/5228-5230).

# Primary mtalk hosts used by Android / FCM long-lived connections.
DOMAIN,alt1-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN,alt2-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN,alt3-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN,alt4-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN,alt5-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN,alt6-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN,alt7-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN,alt8-mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN,mtalk.google.com
DOMAIN,mtalk4.google.com
DOMAIN,mtalk-dev.google.com
DOMAIN,mtalk-staging.google.com

# Internal mobile-gtalk frontend names.
DOMAIN,mobile-gtalk.l.google.com
DOMAIN,alt1.mobile-gtalk.l.google.com
DOMAIN,alt2.mobile-gtalk.l.google.com
DOMAIN,alt3.mobile-gtalk.l.google.com
DOMAIN,alt4.mobile-gtalk.l.google.com
DOMAIN,alt5.mobile-gtalk.l.google.com
DOMAIN,alt6.mobile-gtalk.l.google.com
DOMAIN,alt7.mobile-gtalk.l.google.com
DOMAIN,alt8.mobile-gtalk.l.google.com

# Related Google / Firebase endpoints commonly hit during device registration
# and push setup (not the long-lived mtalk socket itself).
DOMAIN,android.apis.google.com
DOMAIN,device-provisioning.googleapis.com
DOMAIN,firebaseinstallations.googleapis.com

# Host-level IPv4 addresses observed for mtalk/FCM (often ending in .188).
# Kept as /32 because these are individual service IPs, not a published FCM
# CIDR block. no-resolve avoids DNS lookups just for IP-rule matching.
IP-CIDR,64.233.177.188/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,64.233.186.188/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,64.233.187.188/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,64.233.188.188/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,64.233.189.188/32,no-resolve
